course: dictionary
lesson: 2566
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean different things in different places. The same word can describe a young person in a news story and a late bill in a letter. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which is the context, and ask which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: A delinquent is a young person who keeps breaking the law or behaving badly. In a news story about a young person in trouble with the police, the word is used this way. It is a serious word, so writers choose it carefully.
explain: In a bank or business letter, «delinquent» means something else. A «delinquent account» is a bill that has not been paid on time. The clue is the money: nobody is breaking the law, the payment is just late. Look at the topic first, and the right meaning is usually easy to spot.
fact: Delinquent can be a noun (a delinquent) or an adjective (delinquent behaviour).
fact: «Delinquent behaviour» means behaviour that breaks laws or rules.
fact: «Delinquent account» is a formal phrase, mainly used in the US, for a debt that has not been paid on time.
fact: «Juvenile delinquent» means a young person who keeps breaking the law or behaving badly.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: The bank wrote, «Your account is delinquent.» What does delinquent mean here? | A bank that is closed for the day | A young person breaking the law | *A debt that has not been paid on time | A very happy customer
exercise: The report said the «delinquent behaviour» had gone on for months. What does delinquent behaviour mean? | *Behaviour that breaks laws or rules | Behaviour that is always on time | Behaviour that is very kind | Behaviour that is too quiet to hear
exercise: Which phrase names a debt that has not been paid on time? | Juvenile delinquent | *Delinquent account | Glowing account | Delinquent behaviour
test: Jayden reads, «The news story was about a juvenile delinquent who kept breaking the law.» What is a juvenile delinquent? | A bank worker | A very old building | *A young person who keeps breaking the law or behaving badly | A person who pays bills early
test: Nadia reads a letter: «Your payment is delinquent.» Which meaning fits best? | Paid in coins | Paid early | *Not paid on time | Lost in the post
exam: Which sentence uses delinquent to mean a late bill? | *Your delinquent account needs paying by Friday | The delinquent boy was taken home by a police officer | The delinquent shop sells old maps | Delinquent is a word for a happy dog
